// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CANONICAL DATA MODEL — Private Credit Deal Room & Dashboard
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// A clean-slate reference model for a deal room and its dashboard. It is an
// OVERLAY: it owns the workflow and the cross-cutting state — pipeline, team
// and access, data room, committee decisions, covenant monitoring, fund
// positions, alerts and the history dashboards trend — and it LINKS to the
// systems of record for everything else. Borrowers, sponsors, advisors and
// lenders live in the entity master; instruments and their loan terms in the
// security master; collateral in the collateral system; market data with its
// vendor. Those are read through links, never copied here.
//
// Target: PostgreSQL (native enums, Decimal money, partial/composite indexes).
// This is a DESIGN ARTIFACT — it is intentionally separate from the running
// app schema at prisma/schema.prisma and generates to its own client output
// so it can never clobber the live client. See README.md in this directory.
//
// Modeling rules applied throughout:
//   1. Money is Decimal(20,4) — never Float. Ratios are Decimal(18,6).
//   2. Anything a dashboard trends over time is an EVENT TABLE, not a mutable
//      scalar (stage, rating, marks, document versions). Term history such
//      as repricings is the security master's, read through the link.
//   3. Every actor is a User FK — no free-text name strings.
//   4. Multi-tenant: root aggregates carry orgId.
//   5. Amounts always travel with a currency. FX rates are market data, read
//      from the vendor at the time of the roll-up.
//   8. Calendar dates are @db.Date — period ends, as-of, due and effective
//      dates. A timestamp at UTC midnight reads as the previous day anywhere
//      west of Greenwich.
//   6. Real-world identifiers (CUSIP, LoanX, LEI, …) are effective-dated rows
//      in InstrumentIdentifier, never nullable columns on the thing they name.
//   7. Systems of record are linked, never copied. A link row holds a local id
//      (so foreign keys work), orgId and the record's masterRef — no names,
//      descriptions, terms or valuations of the thing it points at.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
  output   = "../../node_modules/.prisma/canonical-client"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("CANONICAL_DATABASE_URL")
}

